{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod `notifications-worker-6784d8b8df-lk5l8` container log reports `ERROR notifications-worker: missing required setting SMTP_PASSWORD (environment variable is unset or empty)`.\n2. Deployment `notifications-worker` references `secretKeyRef` key `SMTP_PASSWORD` with `optional: true` from secret `notifications-smtp`.\n3. Deployment change log CI-2398 documents that Secret `notifications-smtp` holds key `smtp-password`, mismatching the newly required uppercase key from CI-2459.\n\n### Ruled-out Leads\n1. Pod memory exhaustion or OOM killing was ruled out because container status shows termination reason `Error` with exit code 1.\n2. Probe failures causing initial container crash were ruled out because the application process crashed during startup validation before readiness checks.\n\n### Root Cause\nRelease CI-2459 updated the deployment to reference secret key `SMTP_PASSWORD`, but secret `notifications-smtp` contains key `smtp-password`.\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe notifications team should update the deployment `secretKeyRef` key to `smtp-password` or align the secret key name.",
